Source: https://github.com/googleapis/genai-toolbox at a5dc5d4bb03ad2c724f9d6b2a2452307a593a29f,
internal/tools/bigquery/bigquerycommon/table_name_parser.go.

What is adapted from it here: the states of its GoogleSQL lexer (single, double,
triple and raw strings; `--`, `#` and `/* */` comments) and the way it reads a
dotted path whose parts may be backquoted and may have comments between them
(parseIdentifierSequence), in internal/controlplane/bigquery/lexer.go. The
tokens it gives and the refusals made from them (one statement, the keywords
and function paths refused, the `#legacySQL` directive) are Hypomnema's own
(issue #976, design v3, decision 8).

What is learned from it, with no code of its copied: a dry run before every
query and the statement type it reports (internal/tools/bigquery/
bigqueryexecutesql/bigqueryexecutesql.go), the dry run's fields
(bigquerycommon/util.go, DryRunQuery), labelling each job with the tool that
ran it, and testing against an httptest server with option.WithEndpoint.
